    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, which is the only test in the project) passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after defaulting the registration date and before saving, the code is assigned via a new helper:\n   ```java\n   owner.setCustomerCode(generateCustomerCode(owner.getLastName()));\n   ```\n   `generateCustomerCode` builds `LAST3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and `NNNN` as `String.format(\"%04d\", clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1)` \u2014 one more than the current owner count, giving a global zero-padded sequence.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the hsqldb seed uses positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I appended a trailing `NULL` for the new column to each of the 10 owner rows (the other dialects already use explicit column lists).\n\nThe test verifies both the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two sequentially created owners get consecutive numbers \u2014 both pass.",
